 "honest_headline_sentence": "Under equal weight per benchmark cell (8 cells, 1/8 each), the accuracy-max setting beats always-32B-direct on accuracy by +0.0128 [+0.0056, +0.0200] -- but it now costs 1.41x that baseline's compute, not less, and the compute-lean setting neither matches it on the multiple-choice half (-0.0070 [-0.0126, -0.0017], a SIGNIFICANT LOSS) nor stays cheap (1.20x compute, up from 0.49x sample-weighted); the one baseline the method still clearly beats at equal weight is a 32B actually made to reason (+0.0720 [+0.0614, +0.0824] accuracy, -89% latency, -87% energy -- though not fewer FLOP-eq: 1.41x as charged, 1.13x honestly re-costed)."
